adjudication.rationale:
In apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts the auth gate is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset, it evaluates to `undefined`. If the request omits the header, `req.headers[...]` is also `undefined`. The comparison becomes `undefined !== undefined` which is false, so the handler does NOT return 403 and continues processing. That is a fail-open authentication bypass when the secret is not configured, which is a real defect introduced/visible in the diff. (Impact depends on other envs like the encryption key, but the bypass itself is verifiable from the code.)
